{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.eq_of_root_family_agreement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.eq_of_root_family_agreement","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.lean#L92-L111","doc":"**The root family triggers rigidity.** If the gauge-row polynomial `bwPoly` and\nthe value-map polynomial `valPoly` agree at every level-`N` fold value and both have\ndegree `< N − 1`, then they are equal — hence agree at the substrate `t₀`.  The\nantecedent is the concrete *root-of-unity agreement* (the WRT invariant equals the\nmodular datum at each fibre root); by `KeystoneGaugeRowRigidity` this pins the\ncontinuation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.foldPoints_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.foldPoints_card","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.lean#L85-L90","doc":"The finset of level-`N` fold values `{2cos(kπ/N) : 1 ≤ k ≤ N−1}` has exactly\n`N − 1` elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.foldValue_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.foldValue_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.lean#L61-L83","doc":"**The fold values are distinct.** `k ↦ 2cos(kπ/N)` is injective on `[1, N−1]`,\nbecause `cos` is strictly antitone on `[0, π]` and `k ↦ kπ/N` is injective there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.angle_mem_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.angle_mem_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.lean#L52-L59","doc":"The angle `kπ/N` lies in `[0, π]` when `k ≤ N` (and `0 < N`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.foldValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.foldValue","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHabiroRootFamily.lean#L48-L50","doc":"The fold value of the level-`N`, index-`k` fibre root: `t_k = ζ + ζ⁻¹ =\n2cos(kπ/N)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}